v class="QYaTx0tHZZIBm0gZRzJf"><span class="vd1aWiYRdRn48fpbDJ0_"><span role="img" aria-label="ui-icons-star-filled" style="--icon-src: url('https://a.poki-cdn.com/icons/ui-masks/ui-icons-star-filled.svg');" class="kzPaMiKIK5c1hyP3aSiu AfaGcDcSKpA3JuDfG9Ye fcfViJboVjIxhb1F278U"></span>4.3</span><span id="description-votes-count" class="vd1aWiYRdRn48fpbDJ0_">3,475,235 votes</span></div></div><picture class="wIGewHYOM_yiDgJbC_XN"><source srcSet="https://img.poki-cdn.com/cdn-cgi/image/q=78,scq=50,width=314,height=314,fit=cover,f=auto/4abc77cf2ca8a1ca37416249429501f4/drive-mad.png 1x, https://img.poki-cdn.com/cdn-cgi/image/q=78,scq=50,width=628,height=628,fit=cover,f=auto/4abc77cf2ca8a1ca37416249429501f4/drive-mad.png 2x" media="(min-width: 991px)" width="314" height="314" class="bfq4PKbgNwePswLuaSwZ" /><img alt="Drive Mad" src="https://img.poki-cdn.com/cdn-cgi/image/q=78,scq=50,width=204,height=204,fit=cover,f=auto/4abc77cf2ca8a1ca37416249429501f4/drive-mad.png" srcSet="https://img.poki-cdn.com/cdn-cgi/image/q=78,scq=50,width=204,height=204,fit=cover,f=auto/4abc77cf2ca8a1ca37416249429501f4/drive-mad.png 1x, https://img.poki-cdn.com/cdn-cgi/image/q=78,scq=50,width=408,height=408,fit=cover,f=auto/4abc77cf2ca8a1ca37416249429501f4/drive-mad.png 2x" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="204" height="204" class="bfq4PKbgNwePswLuaSwZ" /></picture><div class="U5UHxulLIj1mqRNKVoIl"><p>In Drive Mad, <strong>balance matters more than speed</strong>. Going fast in this physics-based <a onclick="window.navigateTo('/en/car');return false;" href="https://poki.com/en/car">Car Games</a> feels tempting, but <strong>staying in control</strong> keeps the car upright through jumps and landings.</p>
<p>With over <strong>2.5 million player upvotes</strong>, Drive Mad stands out as a <strong>Poki exclusive</strong> built for players looking for that "<em>just one more round</em>" feeling.</p>
<h2>How to play Drive Mad</h2>
<p>To Play Drive Mad, you need to <strong>master braking and acceleration</strong>. The car tilts forward when you accelerate and backward when you brake. Use this to control your angle mid-air and on slopes.</p>
<p>The first <strong>10-15 levels teach balance</strong> and timing. After that, the difficulty ramps up so you better learn from your mistakes fast.</p>
<h3>Controls</h3>
<p>There are only 2 controls to master: <strong>acceleration and braking/reversing.</strong> This simplicity means mistakes show up fast, so timing matters.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Desktop:</strong> Press the right key to move forward and the left key to move backwards.</li>
<li><strong>Mobile:</strong> Tap and hold the arrows to move forward and backwards.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Short taps</strong> let you save bad landings and turn near-crashes into perfect runs. <strong>Hold the button</strong> too long and momentum takes over, turning a clean run into a crash in seconds.</p>
<h2>Drive Mad features</h2>
<p>Each feature changes how the level plays, <strong>catching you out when you get comfortable</strong>.</p>
<h3>Levels and worlds</h3>
<p>Drive Mad has <strong>3 worlds and 250 levels</strong>. To finish them all, you need to land the car safely because later levels don't give you time to fix mistakes.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Classic world:</strong> This is the main Drive Mad experience, with <strong>200 levels</strong> that slowly increase in difficulty.</li>
<li><strong>Winter world:</strong> This winter-themed world adds a snowy aesthetic to the game with <strong>25 different levels</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>Monster truck world:</strong> This world includes <strong>25 levels</strong> where you drive a monster truck with much larger wheels. The added weight makes small mistakes harder to correct, especially in the later stages.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Level mechanics</h3>
<p>These <strong>5 common level mechanics</strong> punish repeating the same move and force you to play each level differently.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Magnet levels:</strong> Drive too close and magnets pull the car, demanding instant corrections to avoid crashing.</li>
<li><strong>Low or zero gravity levels:</strong> Braking shifts the car's balance instead of slowing it down, making timing more important than speed.</li>
<li><strong>Moving machinery levels:</strong> Rotating wheels, conveyors, and swinging obstacles knock the car off balance if you enter at the wrong moment.</li>
<li><strong>Hazard timing levels:</strong> Lasers, shockwaves, and falling objects punish rushed runs and reward patience.</li>
<li><strong>Goal-based puzzle levels</strong>: Pushing objects and creating pathways from obstacles requires controlled movement rather than raw momentum.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Trophies</h3>
<p>There are <strong>24 trophies</strong> to collect in Drive Mad. These trophies <strong>reward players who keep coming back</strong>. They track everything from having 100 total crashes to completing 50 levels in a row without crashing.</p>
<p>There are a number of <strong>level-specific trophies</strong> as well, such as beating level 1 on your back wheels. These trophies give <strong>experienced players</strong> a reason to keep pushing long after the main levels stop being enough.</p>
<h3>Gold time</h3>
<p>Gold time sets a <strong>faster target</strong> that leaves almost no room for hesitation. One extra correction or a slow landing costs it.</p>
<p>While playing a level, a <strong>golden bar</strong> at the bottom of the screen counts down to zero. Beat the level <strong>before it empties</strong> to earn gold time for that stage.</p>
<p>Once a level turns gold, anything less starts to feel unfinished.</p>
<h2>About Drive Mad</h2>
<p>Drive Mad is part of the <a href="https://martinmagni.com/">Martin Magni game collection</a>. The game builds on ideas and mechanics first developed on the <a href="https://www.fancade.com/">Fancade platform</a>.</p>
<p>Since its release in 2019, Drive Mad has been <strong>played over 300,000,000 times</strong>, according to Fancade.</p>
<h3>Drive Mad app</h3>
<p>In addition to the browser version, Drive Mad is available as a mobile app. You can download it on both <strong>iOS and Android.</strong></p>
<h2>Games like Drive Mad</h2>
<p>If you enjoy Drive Mad, you'll likely enjoy other skill-based physics games where clean control matters more than speed.</p>
